-- `l4 run` and `l4 batch` name a different number of failures here, and both
-- exit 0. `l4 batch` prints the module and checks it again, and the printer
-- writes `(signs RAND signs) RAND late` without its brackets, which reads
-- back as `signs RAND (signs RAND late)`. #817's names-once merge depends on
-- that grouping, so `l4 run` names Alice once and `l4 batch` twice; unstable
-- names her twice under both. This is #817's behaviour, made visible by the
-- blame list, not the port's (the adversarial pass of 2026-11-20, F1; NOTE
-- [The same breach on both sides is named once] in L4.EvaluateLazy.Machine).
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob, Carol, Dave
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF deliver, notify, ship, exercise

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`signs` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 8

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`late` MEANS PARTY Bob MUST ship WITHIN 5

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`root` MEANS (`signs` RAND `signs`) RAND `late`

#TRACE `root` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Dave DOES exercise AT 40

@export default trivial entry point, so l4 batch has a function to call
zzT MEANS TRUE
